> It's difficult to determine since I don't know what commands you used (I'm assuming you adapted what I showed earlier, but I can't be sure of that), what your data looks like, or what versions of R and poppr you have installed.
>
> > On Sep 26, 2018, at 14:51 , Palvi Malik <pallv...@gmail.com> wrote:
> >
> > Thanks a lot for the answers and links. You mentioned that you would expect a different output from what I got. What can be the reason for different output? Is there any error in the code?
